amic_bfs_s2, --harness enlcode, --goal","status":"completed","priority":"high"},{"content":"Read program.md in the workspace in full","status":"completed","priority":"high"},{"content":"Implement correct dynamic BFS in candidate.py","status":"in_progress","priority":"high"},{"content":"Run checks (max 8), iterate to full correctness","status":"pending","priority":"high"},{"content":"Run final check (evoalgo check --final) then evoalgo finish","status":"pending","priority":"high"}],"truncated":false},"title":"3 todos","time":{"start":1792505760896,"end":1792505760911}},"id":"prt_159ab44dd001kVDu6hpjRTaTjQ","sessionID":"ses_ea65b95a4ffeXJOPLCkUOttkq1","messageID":"msg_159a692de001guVGgMJbzBEEBg"}}
{"type":"text","timestamp":1792505760928,"sessionID":"ses_ea65b95a4ffeXJOPLCkUOttkq1","part":{"id":"prt_159ab3e9e001iIRBgev4VXK0vy","messageID":"msg_159a692de001guVGgMJbzBEEBg","sessionID":"ses_ea65b95a4ffeXJOPLCkUOttkq1","type":"text","text":"\n\nI now fully understand the mechanics:\n- **State contract**: dict with `parent` and `distances` (lists/dicts indexed by vertex).\n- **Invariant**: valid BFS tree (parent is a true in-neighbor one level closer), spans exactly the reachable set, and reported distances must equal true BFS distances.\n- **Work ratio** = candidate wall-clock / offline-baseline wall-clock. The offline baseline is a full O(n²) BFS on *every* call, so an incremental update that's O(1) for non-tree-edge changes and only recomputes the affected subtree on tree-edge deletion will score well below 1.\n\nLet me update my todos and write the implementation.\n\n","time":{"start":1792505757342,"end":1792505760918}}}
