{"type":"text","timestamp":1792506053910,"sessionID":"ses_ea65b95a4ffeXJOPLCkUOttkq1","part":{"id":"prt_159af9b75001Hqx0IQhtvPZuFd","messageID":"msg_159ab4fcd001TdrDwgw0ceJGUU","sessionID":"ses_ea65b95a4ffeXJOPLCkUOttkq1","type":"text","text":"\n\nNow I understand the mechanics fully. Key facts:\n- **State**: dict with `parent` and `distances` (lists). The checker validates the parent is a true in-neighbor one level closer, the tree spans exactly the reachable set, and reported distances equal true BFS distances.\n- **Work ratio** = candidate wall-time / offline-baseline wall-time, summed over every operation. The baseline does a full O(n²) BFS on *every* call, so fast paths that avoid recomputation drive the ratio well below 1.\n\nMy design: fast path (O(1)) when the update can't change the BFS tree (non-tree-edge insert, or non-tree-edge delete); slow path recomputes only the affected region (reachable-from-v on insert, subtree-of-v on delete) via a boundary-seeded Dijkstra. Let me write it.\n\n","time":{"start":1792506043253,"end":1792506053903}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1792506053943,"sessionID":"ses_ea65b95a4ffeXJOPLCkUOttkq1","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"write","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-80ad7ee6f0022371","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/home/ethomdt/thesis/runs/eval1_harness_dynamic_bfs_s2/candidate.py","content":"\"\"\"Dynamic BFS tree from a fixed root (vertex 0) under edge flips.\n\nState is a dict with two list fields, indexed by vertex:\n  parent[v]    - the BFS-tree parent of v (None for the root and for\n                 unreachable vertices)\n  distances[v] - the true BFS distance from the root (-1 if unreachable)\n\nFast path: an update that cannot change the BFS tree returns immediately.\n  * insert (u, v): if u is unreachable, or dist[v] <= dist[u] + 1, the new\n    edge gives no shorter path, so nothing changes.\n  * delete (u, v): if (u, v) is not v's tree edge (parent[v] != u), no vertex\n    loses its tree path, so nothing changes.\n\nSlow path: only the affected region is recomputed, never the whole graph.\n  * insert that improves v: region = vertices reachable from v (their distance\n    can only drop through the new edge).\n  * delete of v's tree edge: region = the subtree of v (the only vertices\n    whose tree path used the deleted edge).\n\nThe region is recomputed with a boundary-seeded Dijkstra: vertices outside the\nregion keep their (unchanged) distances, and the new distance of a region\nvertex is the shortest path from the boundary into it. Because every out-\nneighbor of a reachable vertex is itself reachable, and a vertex's distance is\nset by its in-neighbors, this is exact for both regions.\n\"\"\"\n\nimport heapq\n\n\ndef init(graph):\n    n = len(graph)\n    parent, dist = _full_bfs(graph, n, 0)\n    return {\"parent\": parent, \"distances\": dist}\n\n\ndef insert_edge(graph, edge, state):\n    u, v = edge\n    dist = state[\"distances\"]\n    parent = state[\"parent\"]\n    n = len(dist)\n    if dist[u] == -1:\n        return state  # u unreachable: no path root -> ... -> u -> v\n    if dist[v] != -1 and dist[v] <= dist[u] + 1:\n        return state  # new edge gives no shorter path to v\n    region = _reachable_from(graph, n, v)\n    region.discard(0)  # the root's distance is fixed at 0\n    _recompute(graph, n, region, dist, parent)\n    return state\n\n\ndef delete_edge(graph, edge, state):\n    u, v = edge\n    parent = state[\"parent\"]\n    dist = state[\"distances\"]\n    n = len(dist)\n    if parent[v] != u:\n        return state  # (u, v) is not v's tree edge: no tree path is lost\n    region = _subtree_of(parent, n, v)\n    region.discard(0)\n    _recompute(graph, n, region, dist, parent)\n    return state\n\n\ndef _full_bfs(graph, n, root):\n    from collections import deque\n\n    parent = [None] * n\n    dist = [-1] * n\n    dist[root] = 0\n    q = deque([root])\n    while q:\n        u = q.popleft()\n        row = graph[u]\n        nd = dist[u] + 1\n        for v in range(n):\n            if row[v] == 1 and dist[v] == -1:\n                dist[v] = nd\n                parent[v] = u\n                q.append(v)\n    return parent, dist\n\n\ndef _reachable_from(graph, n, start):\n    \"\"\"All vertices reachable from start by following out-edges (incl. start).\"\"\"\n    from collections import deque\n\n    seen = {start}\n    q = deque([start])\n    while q:\n        u = q.popleft()\n        row = graph[u]\n        for v in range(n):\n            if row[v] == 1 and v not in seen:\n                seen.add(v)\n                q.append(v)\n    return seen\n\n\ndef _subtree_of(parent, n, v):\n    \"\"\"v and all its descendants in the tree, found by walking parent chains.\"\"\"\n    region = set()\n    for x in range(n):\n        cur = x\n        while cur is not None:\n            if cur == v:\n                region.add(x)\n                break\n            cur = parent[cur]\n    return region\n\n\ndef _recompute(graph, n, region, dist, parent):\n    \"\"\"Recompute distances/parents for the vertices in region in place.\n\n    Vertices outside region keep their current (final) distances. The new\n    distance of a region vertex is the shortest path from the boundary (its\n    in-neighbors outside region) into it, so a Dijkstra seeded from the\n    boundary and relaxing only inside region is exact.\n    \"\"\"\n    best = {}\n    heap = []\n    for x in region:\n        b = None\n        for w in range(n):\n            if graph[w][x] == 1 and w not in region and dist[w] != -1:\n                cand = dist[w] + 1\n                if b is None or cand < b:\n                    b = cand\n        if b is not None:\n            best[x] = b\n            heapq.heappush(heap, (b, x))\n\n    final = {}\n    while heap:\n        d, w = heapq.heappop(heap)\n        if w in final:\n            continue\n        final[w] = d\n        row = graph[w]\n        for x in range(n):\n            if row[x] == 1 and x in region and x not in final:\n                cand = d + 1\n                if x not in best or cand < best[x]:\n                    best[x] = cand\n                    heapq.heappush(heap, (cand, x))\n\n    for x in region:\n        dist[x] = final[x] if x in final else -1\n    for x in region:\n        if dist[x] == -1:\n            parent[x] = None\n            continue\n        p = None\n        for w in range(n):\n            if graph[w][x] == 1 and dist[w] + 1 == dist[x]:\n                p = w\n                break\n        parent[x] = p\n"},"output":"Wrote file successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"filepath":"/home/ethomdt/thesis/runs/eval1_harness_dynamic_bfs_s2/candidate.py","exists":true,"truncated":false},"title":"runs/eval1_harness_dynamic_bfs_s2/candidate.py","time":{"start":1792506053892,"end":1792506053935}},"id":"prt_159afa0c4001qDHnyLaG4kDB3c","sessionID":"ses_ea65b95a4ffeXJOPLCkUOttkq1","messageID":"msg_159ab4fcd001TdrDwgw0ceJGUU"}}
