{"type":"text","timestamp":1792506307207,"sessionID":"ses_ea65b95a4ffeXJOPLCkUOttkq1","part":{"id":"prt_159b3994d0015z2YrTbuwxwiST","messageID":"msg_159b2b04f0010r8B5CrDFkY1LA","sessionID":"ses_ea65b95a4ffeXJOPLCkUOttkq1","type":"text","text":"\n\nExcellent — all 1600 random sequences pass (n=2..5, 400 seeds each, 30 ops each), and my checker mirrors the real `check_invariant` closely. My correctness proof: the Dijkstra solution equals the true BFS distances because (a) any boundary-seeded in-region path is a real root-to-x path, so `final[x] >= true_dist[x]`, and (b) by induction on finalization order `true_dist[x] >= final[x]`. Now let me run the authoritative evoalgo check (check 1 of 8).\n\n","time":{"start":1792506304845,"end":1792506307199}}}
