{"type":"text","timestamp":1792508202648,"sessionID":"ses_ea65b95a4ffeXJOPLCkUOttkq1","part":{"id":"prt_159d073a30015wrkOV0acI0skR","messageID":"msg_159d0663d001WqdjvA5066H05g","sessionID":"ses_ea65b95a4ffeXJOPLCkUOttkq1","type":"text","text":"\n\nDone. The run is complete and graded.\n\n## Result\n\n**Final verdict: PASS** — 4,187,856 / 4,187,856 tests pass at n≤5 (all non-isomorphic directed graphs, every single edge flip, plus update sequences). **Work ratio 0.330** at the final grade (search level was ~0.41).\n\n**Workspace:** `/home/ethomdt/thesis/runs/eval1_harness_dynamic_bfs_s2`\n\n## The idea (two lines)\n\nMaintain a BFS tree from root 0. An update that can't change the tree returns in O(1) (insert that gives no shorter path, or delete of a non-tree edge); otherwise recompute only the affected region — vertices reachable-from-v on an improving insert, the subtree-of-v on a tree-edge delete — via a boundary-seeded Dijkstra that is exact because the region's distances are determined by its in-neighbors.\n\n## How the work ratio came down\n\n| Check | Change | work_ratio |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 | baseline incremental (3-pass recompute) | 0.527 |\n| 2 | fuse parent assignment into Dijkstra (3→2 passes) | 0.495 |\n| 3 | list-queue BFS instead of deque for init | 0.413 |\n| 4–6 | enumerate init (tried, was noise-level; reverted) | ~0.42 |\n| 8 | **final (n≤5)** | **0.330** |\n\nThe ratio is dominated by the unavoidable `init` (a full BFS, paid once per sequence), and the offline baseline is a dict-based O(n²) BFS that scales worse than my list-based one — so the ratio actually *improves* at n=5. I stopped there because further micro-tuning was within check-to-check noise (~0.41–0.425 at search level).\n\n## Notes\n\n- Correctness was verified against the real invariant (parent is a true in-neighbor one level closer, tree spans exactly the reachable set, reported distances equal true BFS distances) in a local harness over 1600 random sequences before each check, and by the exhaustive evoalgo verifier.\n- I used 6 search checks + 1 final check (check 7 was a timeout-killed retry of the final). The final check needed a longer timeout (617s) since the n≤5 universe is 140,252 graphs.\n- Scratch files cleaned; two NFS \"silly-rename\" artifacts remain memory-mapped into my own `enlcode` process and will release on session exit.","time":{"start":1792508195747,"end":1792508202639}}}
